course: dictionary
lesson: 7814
title: Quickly: fast, soon or without waiting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quickly is an adverb. It tells you how, when or how fast something happens. In «Run quickly!» it tells you how to run. Adverbs often end in -ly, and they can take more and most: more quickly, most quickly.
explain: Quickly has three meanings. It can mean at a fast speed, as in «Run quickly!». It can mean in a short time, or soon, as in «The ice melted quickly.». It can mean without waiting, as in «He quickly said sorry.». Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a different word. In «The ice melted quickly», soon fits, so it means in a short time. In «He quickly said sorry», straight away fits, so it means without waiting. If your swap makes no sense, try another meaning.
fact: Quickly is an adverb, so it tells you how, when or how fast something happens.
fact: «Quickly» means at a fast speed, in a short time, or without waiting.
fact: Things that change quickly change a lot in a short time, which is why scientists and mathematicians use the word to describe rates.
fact: In a fire, leave quickly but calmly. Near a pool, do not run quickly.
fact: Giant anteaters flick a sticky tongue about 60 centimetres long up to about 150 times a minute, so they feed quickly at each nest.
exercise: What does quickly mean in «Run quickly!»? | *At a fast speed | In a short time, soon | Very loudly | Without waiting
exercise: «The ice melted quickly.» What does quickly mean here? | *In a short time, soon | At a fast speed, like running | Very cold | Without waiting for anyone
exercise: «He quickly said sorry.» What does quickly mean here? | *Without waiting, straight away | Very loudly | At a fast speed, like running
test: Salt from sea spray makes iron rust quickly by the sea. Quickly here means: | Very loudly | At a fast speed, like running | *In a short time, soon | Without waiting for you
test: Which form is correct? Tom ran ___ than Sam. | *more quickly | quickest | quick | quicklier
exam: Which sentence uses quickly to mean without waiting? | «Run quickly to the bus!» | «The flip book looked quick.» | *«He quickly said sorry.» | «The ice melted quickly.»
